    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "AND2",
        "Description": "NOT reading (input A, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.375) of the shipped 'Logic Gate NOT-NAND' gate. Role in the ALU: second stage of the AND datapath, Y = NOT(AND1.Y) = A AND B \u2014 the result the MUX selects when Op = 0, feeding NANDA.A. The whole ALU composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate's truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction \u2014 there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of A, B and Op onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit through its persisted signal name); the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in 'Logic Gate Half Adder').",
