      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "NOT1",
        "Description": "NOT reading (input A, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.375) of the shipped 'Logic Gate NOT-NAND' gate. Role in the ALU: select inversion of the shipped 2-to-1 MUX composition, Y = NOT(Op), feeding NANDA.B. Its A pin reads the select toggle through the signal name Op at the logic layer. The whole ALU composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate's truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction \u2014 there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of A, B and Op onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit through its persisted signal name); the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in 'Logic Gate Half Adder').",
        "Identifier": "group_f8b3c69b530c4c4b87ad8cd761008b66",
        "IdGuid": "a392c740-7039-42f8-ad04-4defd260083b",
